      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_22fd8f35c507b2ae28a370ea19e99088fe6d9d4677119276e29bb1e4f845c9ff",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The largest prime p acts as a coordinate for the ambient size of an SA number because its exponent constraints force a nearly complete stack of prime-power contributions below p. Chebyshev functions compress that stack into a tractable analytic quantity.",
