    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b8393366723a0b3777cc3395ed14efc99b3611618d2dec64fe47365c2986e13f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The conditional theorem supplies an analytic target for the finite local-regularity data: nondecreasing largest prime and sufficiently large consecutive-XA spacing control the competing sigma/n gain and phi/n loss, while the observed bounded exponent-vector transitions describe the neighboring factorizations on which that competition occurs. The separately computed ratio and composition monotonicities therefore form a falsifiable family of tests for whether this local rigidity persists under changes of arithmetic representation.",
